  "body": "Found while deciding #18. Public Heidenhain TNC 620/640 DIN/ISO programming manuals (as read through cited summaries, not yet the PDF itself) describe I/J/K in this dialect as the circle centre in absolute coordinates. assets/posts/heidenhain.cps writes XY-arc I/J as centre minus start (the Fanuc incremental meaning), and the arc_planes goldens lock that output.\n\nIf the manual reading holds, a real TNC would place every XY arc's centre wrongly - wrong output on the machine (P0).\n\nDone means: verify the I/J meaning against the manual PDF itself; if absolute, emit absolute centre words (or the dialect's documented incremental form), regenerate the Heidenhain goldens with a reviewed diff, and pin it with a test that reconstructs the centre from the posted words; if incremental is correct, close with the manual page cited.",
